# Flip Wars - Complete Game Analysis

## 📋 Project Overview

**Flip Wars** is a strategic tile-flipping game that demonstrates **Divide & Conquer (D&C)** algorithms for a DAA (Design & Analysis of Algorithms) course project.

| Attribute | Value |
|-----------|-------|
| Grid Sizes | 4×4, 5×5, 6×6 |
| Players | Human (Yellow) vs CPU (Grey) |
| Win Condition | Conquer all tiles OR highest score at turn limit |
| Turn Limit | 15 (4×4) or 25 (5×5, 6×6) |

---

## 🔄 Game Workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A[Game Start] --> B[Random Initial Setup]
    B --> C[Player Turn]
    C --> D{Click Tile}
    D -->|Locked| E[Show Error]
    E --> C
    D -->|Valid| F[Flip + Pattern]
    F --> G[Lock Tile in Tabu List]
    G --> H{Check Win?}
    H -->|Yes| I[Game Over]
    H -->|No| J[CPU Turn]
    J --> K[AI Evaluates All Moves]
    K --> L[Merge Sort Ranks Moves]
    L --> M[Execute Best Move]
    M --> N{Check Win?}
    N -->|Yes| I
    N -->|No| C
```

---

## 🧠 Algorithms Used

### 1. Merge Sort (Search Space D&C)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Location** | [Engine.java#L44-L70](file:///d:/DAA/src/main/java/com/flipwars/Engine.java#L44-L70) |
| **Time Complexity** | O(n log n) |
| **Space Complexity** | O(n) |

**How It Works:**
```
DIVIDE:   [8,3,5,1,9,2,7,4] → [8,3,5,1] + [9,2,7,4]
          [8,3,5,1] → [8,3] + [5,1]
          ...until single elements

CONQUER:  Compare pairs: 8>3, 5>1, 9>2, 7>4

COMBINE:  Merge sorted halves: [8,5,3,1] + [9,7,4,2] → [9,8,7,5,4,3,2,1]
```

**Why Used:**
- Evaluates 16 possible moves, needs efficient sorting
- Stable sort guarantees consistent results
- O(n log n) is optimal for comparison-based sorting

---

### 2. Spatial D&C (Quadrant Evaluation)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Location** | [DACAlgorithms.java#L17-L66](file:///d:/DAA/src/main/java/com/flipwars/DACAlgorithms.java#L17-L66) |
| **Time Complexity** | O(n) where n = grid size² |
| **Space Complexity** | O(1) |

**How It Works:**
```
┌─────┬─────┐
│ TL  │ TR  │  DIVIDE: Split grid into 4 quadrants
├─────┼─────┤  
│ BL  │ BR  │  CONQUER: Score each quadrant = (Grey - Yellow)
└─────┴─────┘  
                COMBINE: Total = 1.5×(TL + TR + BL + BR)
```

**Why Used:**
- Captures positional strategy (corner quadrants matter more)
- Simple recursive subdivision of 2D space
- Demonstrates geometric D&C concept

---

### 3. DFS Clusters (Structural D&C)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Location** | [DACAlgorithms.java#L68-L146](file:///d:/DAA/src/main/java/com/flipwars/DACAlgorithms.java#L68-L146) |
| **Time Complexity** | O(n) where n = tiles |
| **Space Complexity** | O(n) for visited array + recursion stack |

**How It Works:**
```
Grid:           Clusters Found:
█░░█            Island1(size=2): ██
█░█░    DFS→    Island2(size=2): █░
░░█░                              █
░░░█            Island3(size=1): █

DIVIDE:   Split into connected components via DFS
CONQUER:  Score each island = size²
COMBINE:  Sum top 3 largest clusters
```

**Why Used:**
- Connected tiles = stronger position
- Large clusters are hard for opponent to break
- Models "territory control" strategy

---

### 4. Minimax (Temporal D&C)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Location** | [DACAlgorithms.java#L148-L256](file:///d:/DAA/src/main/java/com/flipwars/DACAlgorithms.java#L148-L256) |
| **Time Complexity** | O(b^d) where b=16 moves, d=depth |
| **Space Complexity** | O(d) recursion depth |

**How It Works:**
```
Depth 0 (CPU):     [Current State]
                  /    |    |    \
Depth 1 (Player): [F0] [F1] [...] [F15]  ← 16 futures
                  /|\   /|\
Depth 2 (CPU):   ...   ...        ← Responses

DIVIDE:   Branch into all possible future states
CONQUER:  Evaluate leaf nodes
COMBINE:  Maximizing player picks MAX, minimizing picks MIN
```

**Why Used:**
- Looks ahead to predict opponent's response
- Alpha-Beta pruning cuts branches (O(b^(d/2)) best case)
- Classic game theory algorithm

---

### 5. Tabu Search (Memory/Locking)

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| **Location** | [Rules.java#L9-L43](file:///d:/DAA/src/main/java/com/flipwars/Rules.java#L9-L43) |
| **Time Complexity** | O(k) where k = tabu size |
| **Space Complexity** | O(k) |

**How It Works:**
```
Move History: [3, 7, 12, 5]  ← FIFO queue
              ↑              ↑
           Oldest         Newest
           (unlocks       (locked)
            soon)

When move 9 is played:
[3, 7, 12, 5] → [7, 12, 5, 9]
  ↑ removed
```

**Why Used:**
- Prevents infinite flip loops
- Adds strategic depth (plan around locks)
- Memory-efficient FIFO implementation

---

## ⚖️ Combined Scoring Formula

```java
FinalScore = (Strategic × 0.4) + (Quadrant × 0.2) + (Cluster × 0.2)
// Note: Minimax is available separately via getBestMoveMinimax()
```

| Component | Weight | What It Measures |
|-----------|--------|------------------|
| Strategic | 40% | Tile position values (corners, edges, traps) |
| Quadrant | 20% | Regional control balance |
| Cluster | 20% | Territory connectivity |

